From 806368336f0b0b6ddf8d3a68af81e68072378d97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20Iwanicki?= <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:15:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/28] fix(rdv3): set up the BL31 translation tables on every
 variant
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Since 95230492b ("fix(gic): init the GIC before the platform with a
hook"), rdv3 defines bl31_plat_arch_setup() for every variant, but calls
arm_bl31_plat_arch_setup() only for variant 2. On variants 0 and 1 BL31
then never sets up its translation tables or enables the MMU, which the
weak default in arm_bl31_setup.c does before it sets the GICR frames.

Call arm_bl31_plat_arch_setup() on every variant, before the multi-chip
mappings and the GIC setup.

Signed-off-by: Michał Iwanicki <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
---
 plat/arm/board/neoverse_rd/platform/rdv3/rdv3_bl31_setup.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/arm/board/neoverse_rd/platform/rdv3/rdv3_bl31_setup.c b/plat/arm/board/neoverse_rd/platform/rdv3/rdv3_bl31_setup.c
index 9d329ec93..754ed2e9a 100644
--- a/plat/arm/board/neoverse_rd/platform/rdv3/rdv3_bl31_setup.c
+++ b/plat/arm/board/neoverse_rd/platform/rdv3/rdv3_bl31_setup.c
@@ -152,11 +152,13 @@ static uintptr_t rdv3mc_multichip_gicr_frames[] = {
 
 void __init bl31_plat_arch_setup(void)
 {
-#if (NRD_PLATFORM_VARIANT == 2)
-#if (PLATFORM_NODE_COUNT > 1)
+#if (NRD_PLATFORM_VARIANT == 2) && (PLATFORM_NODE_COUNT > 1)
 	int ret;
 #endif
+
 	arm_bl31_plat_arch_setup();
+
+#if (NRD_PLATFORM_VARIANT == 2)
 #if (PLATFORM_NODE_COUNT > 1)
 	/* Add mmap for all remote chips */
 	for (int i = 1; i < ARRAY_SIZE(per_cpu_nodes_base); i++) {
-- 
2.55.0

